      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CHALK AND CHEESE (3) was safely held in tougher company last start after being shuffled back early at Bendigo, but prior to that won by 2 lengths at Geelong (22.80) beating Miss Jo in a Grade 5 on October 9. Has performed well from this box with a win and five minor placings to his name from 10 starts. Has ability and is a key runner. ZIPPING BANGALOW (1) jumped from a middle draw last time and could manage only fourth and beaten 1.75 lengths (20.35) at Traralgon. Has ability and can atone. PAW QATAR (8) missed the frame and safely held latest finishing 6th at Geelong following on from a win (22.48) at this track the start prior. Has a good record here at this journey. Will give the top chances plenty to think about. JACKALOPE (6) is a chance after winning last time.",
